.TH CNCDECK 1 "2026" "cncdeck" "User commands"
.SH NAME
cncdeck \- G\-code sender for GRBL 1.1 CNCs with an SVG converter
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B cncdeck
[\fB\-\-sim\fR] [\fB\-\-no\-splash\fR] [\fIFILE\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
CNC Deck streams G\-code files to a GRBL 1.1 CNC over a serial port, with a 3D preview,
DRO, jogging, Z probe, overrides, board settings and height\-map leveling. The SVG Converter
mode turns an SVG file into G\-code (outside, inside, pocket, engrave and holding tabs) and
hands it to the sender without saving a file.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.I FILE
G\-code file to open at start\-up.
.TP
.B \-\-sim
Connect to the built\-in GRBL simulator: try it without a machine.
.TP
.B \-\-no\-splash
Do not show the 3 second splash screen (same as CNCDECK_NO_SPLASH=1).
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/cncdeck/cncdeck.conf
User settings (port, jog speed, macros, window geometry).
.TP
.I /usr/share/doc/cncdeck/
Documentation and examples (README.Debian: dialout group and brltty).
.SH AUTHOR
Stefano Ciurleo & Claude Code.
